acceptance_criteria: "Conflicting local edits require explicit decisions; retries are idempotent; rollback uses audited SDK mutations; typed SDK and CLI with compact TOON/JSON, actionable refusals, docs and non-git real-tracker validation."
resolution: "Versioned upgrades preserve local settings, require explicit conflict decisions, retry idempotently and roll back through audited SDK mutations."
expected_result: "Conflicting local edits require explicit decisions; retries are idempotent; rollback uses audited SDK mutations; typed SDK and CLI with compact TOON/JSON, actionable refusals, docs and non-git real-tracker validation."
actual_result: "https://github.com/unbraind/pm-presets/pull/153, merged 2026-10-22T20:16:03Z, merge 0ca9e2a6e7bdde9b069691c22424cf14a3e6ef7d: Versioned upgrades preserve local settings, require explicit conflict decisions, retry idempotently and roll back through audited SDK mutations."
comments[4]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-22T19:20:17.916Z",codex-agent,"Overlap recheck: src/diff.ts compares one preset with current configuration; core SDK config/history provides audited mutations and history reads; core package migrations run extension lifecycle migrations; pm-vcs provides general three-way file/record reconciliation; pm-ops provides operational gates. None models vendor preset versions plus intervening local settings choices. Use mutateWorkspaceSettings locking, includePreview canonical settings, replacement subtrees and operationId replay. New scope: versioned settings-only receipts, explicit local/vendor conflict choices, stale-state guards and audited rollback; no Git required. Keep dependency pin unchanged (2026.10.17); registry currently reports CLI 2026.10.22."
  "2026-10-22T19:32:48.316Z",codex-agent,"Implemented versioned settings-only three-way comparison, private digest-bound recovery receipts, explicit JSON-pointer conflict choices, canonical host previews, audited apply/rollback, stable retries, explicit new generations after rollback, stale-state guards and bounded agent reports. Behavioral revert proof: removing the conflict guard fails the expected refusal; changing stable operation identity to a fresh timestamp fails replay assertion; replacing the settings mutation with a no-op fails the lifecycle regression. Each isolated reversion exited 1; original implementation restored. Real public origin/main tracker validation: certified 75 items, 156 copied files, 76 history streams, 568 history entries; one conflict and one automatic vendor change, repeated resolved plans identical, zero copied file changes. Permission-restricted data required a writable transient locks directory: pinned SDK dry-run acquires workspace-history lock. This host constraint is documented; source checkout was not mutated. Test result tracking is disabled by existing project policy, so linked run evidence is recorded here without changing policy."
  "2026-10-22T19:37:12.144Z",codex-agent,"Local final validation: 9/9 new regression and installed-CLI acceptance tests pass; new source modules measure 100% lines/branches/functions. Existing command, registry and README suites pass 29/29. npm run typecheck, npm run build:test, npm run docstring (48 files, 127 declarations), git diff --check, changelog generation/check and isolated-home strict tracker health pass. No dedicated lint script exists; the configured docstring/static checks and whitespace lint were run. Both linked commands pass via pm test. Additional rollback-only behavioral reversion exits 1, then source restored. Public-copy revalidation retains 75 certified items, 156 unchanged files, 76 history streams and 568 entries. Normal-home health exposes an unrelated global pm-github host-version skew; isolated-home health succeeds without changing the pin or global setup. Full npm and Bun release checks are delegated to the existing CI release-gate job because of shared host load; exact counts/run URL will be recorded in the PR. Acceptance remains in progress for orchestrator verification; claim released."
  "2026-10-22T19:38:36.105Z",codex-agent,"Current CLI overlap confirmation: installed pm --version reports 2026.10.22. Its core upgrade help upgrades CLI/SDK and managed packages (now routed to package upgrade); workspace config exposes typed settings get/set/list/export. Neither accepts two vendor preset revisions or local conflict decisions. This confirms the original pinned-SDK and sibling-package overlap findings against the current CLI command surface."
